# Local dev config.
#
# Locally there is no ISA sign-in configured, so auth/AuthContext.tsx falls
# back to its sessionStorage token (dev-admin-token, or dev-person-token:<name>).
# That is what lets the editing and admin Cypress specs run with no AWS account.
#
# To sign in locally with a real ISA account instead (http://localhost:5173 is a
# registered callback on SlackData's ISA client), copy the three VITE_ISA_*
# lines from .env.production into .env.development.local, and start the API with
# ISA_USER_POOL_ID=eu-central-1_iGaYGKeyJ ISA_CLIENT_ID=2snjdh8i6md0m5n6h9te1hlor1.
#
# Not a security boundary: the server refuses the dev tokens the moment the ISA
# pool is configured, and always when hosted (api/auth.py, deployment.py).
